Original commit body from d2edb70:

The Python fallback was doing N regex searches per file (where N is
the number of symbols). This caused multi-hour processing times on
large repos like TensorFlow.

Fix: build a single combined regex pattern \b(sym1|sym2|...)\b and
use findall() to match all symbols in one pass per file.

Benchmarks (estimated for TensorFlow with ~225K symbols, ~3K files):
- Before: O(225K * 3K) = ~675M regex operations
- After: O(3K) = ~3K regex operations (one per file)
